---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
const updated = '23 July 2026';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Note"
  description="How Not Now Dear handles your data — plainly and briefly."
  showTopbar={true}
>
  <section class="article">
    <div class="shell">
      <header class="article__header" data-reveal>
        <div class="eyebrow">The small print, made small</div>
        <h1>Privacy Note</h1>
        <div class="article__meta"><span>Last updated {updated}</span></div>
      </header>

      <div class="prose" data-reveal>
        <p>
          This note explains, in plain language, what happens to your
          information when you use this website. The short version: we collect as
          little as possible, and we never sell it.
        </p>

        <h2>The mailing list</h2>
        <p>
          If you subscribe, we collect your name, email address and (optionally)
          your country, so we can send you occasional news about the book. Sign-up
          uses <strong>double opt-in</strong> — you'll receive a confirmation
          email and are only added once you click the link inside. You can
          unsubscribe from any email with one click. Our newsletter is managed by
          Buttondown, acting as our data processor.
        </p>

        <h2>Comments</h2>
        <p>
          Comments and reactions on journal posts are powered by Giscus, which
          stores them as GitHub Discussions. To comment you sign in with a GitHub
          account, and your comment is public. Comments are moderated.
        </p>

        <h2>Analytics &amp; cookies</h2>
        <p>
          We use privacy-friendly, cookieless analytics to understand which
          writing readers enjoy — only after you accept via the cookie banner.
          Decline and no analytics load at all. We don't use advertising or
          cross-site tracking cookies.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Under the GDPR and similar laws you can ask to access, correct or delete
          any personal data we hold about you. Just email
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and we'll take care of
          it.
        </p>

        <div class="button-row">
          <a class="button button--ghost" href="/">← Back to home</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
